sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Readiness and data-preserving rollback
  accDescr: After compatibility and artifact checks, the reconciler snapshots the database and applies application images. A SQL-backed readiness check either accepts the new revision or restores the old application and origin images. Database contents are retained.
  participant R as Reconciler
  participant A as Application + origin
  participant D as Database
  Note over R,D: Database / CMS-base changes held for compatibility review
  R->>D: Pre-update snapshot
  D-->>R: Snapshot complete
  R->>A: Apply new images
  R->>A: HTTPS readiness check
  A->>D: Read-only SQL check
  D-->>A: Readiness result
  A-->>R: Health result
  alt Healthy
    R->>R: Record applied revision
  else Failed
    R->>A: Restore old app + origin images
    R->>A: Recheck readiness
    Note over A,D: Database contents preserved<br/>No automatic schema downgrade
  end
